# Prisma & Database Conventions

## Schema Location

Schema: `prisma/schema.prisma`. Generated client output: `src/generated/prisma/` (never edit manually).

## Provider & Adapter

- Provider: `sqlite`
- Runtime adapter: `@prisma/adapter-libsql` with `@libsql/client`
- Dev: local file `file:./prisma/dev.db`
- Prod: Turso remote (`libsql://...` URL + auth token)

## Data Models

| Model | Key Fields | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| `User` | id, email, name | App user (NextAuth managed) |
| `Account` | provider, providerAccountId | OAuth accounts |
| `Session` | sessionToken, expires | DB sessions (JWT used instead) |
| `Symptom` | name, intensity (1-10), occurredAt, notes | Symptom entries |
| `PredefinedSymptom` | name (unique per user) | Saved symptom names for quick entry |
| `Medication` | name, dosage (mg), time (HH:mm), active | Daily medications |
| `MedicationLog` | medicationId, date, takenAt, scheduledAt, deltaMinutes | Daily take log (unique per med+date) |
| `BowelMovement` | bristolType (1-7), occurredAt, notes | Bristol scale entries |
| `SignificantEvent` | text, date (YYYY-MM-DD), time (HH:mm) | Free-text dated significant events |

## Conventions

- All domain models have `userId` FK with `onDelete: Cascade`
- IDs: `@id @default(cuid())`
- Timestamps: `createdAt @default(now())`, `updatedAt @updatedAt` where applicable
- Indexes on `userId`, `occurredAt`, `date`, `name` for query performance
- `MedicationLog` has `@@unique([medicationId, date])` for one log per med per day

## Migrations

Use `npx prisma migrate dev --name <description>` for schema changes. For production Turso, use manual SQL scripts in `scripts/` (SQLite limitations with ALTER TABLE).

## Client Usage

```typescript
import { prisma } from "@/lib/prisma";

const symptoms = await prisma.symptom.findMany({
  where: { userId, occurredAt: { gte: startDate, lte: endDate } },
  orderBy: { occurredAt: "desc" },
});
```
